      "content": "Metal loops attached to a horse's bit, which guide the reins and prevent them from becoming tangled or snagged on the harness. [Source: Getty AAT] | terret, especially each of the two rings by which the leash is attached to the jesses of a hawk (OED s.v. terret b), i.e. to the strap of leather etc. fastened around each of the legs of a hawk (OED s.v. jess n.)"
